IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mvwaci-ciss`

-- Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic Injuries) Act 2016 (WA), with Civil Liability Act 2002 s 13A and Motor
-- Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943 ss 3EA, 3FB -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against
-- a decided case, and no regulations under the Act were retrieved: whether an injury meets the prescribed criteria for a
-- catastrophic injury, or for lifetime participation, is a stated fact in every case.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_motor-vehicle-and-workplace-accidents-catastrophic-injuries-act-2016_baseline.py). Expected results were written by hand
-- from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa): Chloe and Liam license a used car in June 2034, compulsory third
-- party insurance coming with the licence (c074). The cases ask what that cover means for Chloe if she is catastrophically
-- injured: alone in her own car (inside the scheme, no fault needed), or as a passenger while Liam drives negligently
-- (outside it: a common-law claim on the car's CTP policy). The workplace cases are illustrative, not from a life.

§ `fixtures`

`Chloe's licensed car runs off a WA road in 2034, no one else involved` MEANS `The accident` WITH
    `how it happened` IS `the driving of a motor vehicle`
    `it happened in Western Australia` IS TRUE
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2016` IS TRUE
    `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury` IS FALSE
    `it happened on private land` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance` IS TRUE
    `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme` IS FALSE
    `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event` IS FALSE
    `it resulted from a terrorist act` IS FALSE

